KG42.register("nodes-33c447f07363aa5b6bc2370f",{"id":"COMP-c98744ae891e04fd","code":"CLR015","label":"Supply allocation through supply-demand comparison and excess-supply curtailment","definition":"Under the trading scope and matching premises specified by the source, supply acceptance is determined by comparing supply and demand quantities: when there is no excess supply, the full amount is accepted; when there is excess supply, the actual allocated quantity is determined according to the curtailment rule for that scope.","layer":"L5","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"clearing.local","concept_ids":["clearing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"definition":"Under the trading scope and matching premises specified by the source, supply acceptance is determined by comparing supply and demand quantities: when there is no excess supply, the full amount is accepted; when there is excess supply, the actual allocated quantity is determined according to the curtailment rule for that scope.","object":"The allocation relationship from declared or equilibrium supply quantity to actual allocated quantity for supply resources; the energy storage sharing space and order electricity quantity retain their respective types, units, and aggregation scopes.","inputs":"Comparable supply quantities, demand quantities, applicable premises, and source-specified oversupply handling parameters within the same trading scope.","operation":"Within that scope, when supply does not exceed demand, all supply is accepted; when supply exceeds demand, the actual allocated quantity is calculated according to the source-specified oversupply curtailment rules.","outputs":"The actual allocated quantity on the supply side, retaining the distinct output semantics and quantity domains of each RU's shared quantity and the bilateral transaction volumes of an order pair.","boundary":"Limited to L5/DA quantity configuration; energy storage compares the total quantity of the selected group, and CDA compares price-compatible order pairs. One must not infer a common max/min formula, that total group allocation necessarily equals demand, per-demand-side allocation, or common order maintenance rules."},"exclusions":[["The object is the energy storage sharing space provided by J−1 RUs and demanded by K−1 SFCs; the group is determined first, then allocation is executed, with repeated application in the time-slot extension.","Input x_i^* is the equilibrium provision quantity, and q_m is the energy storage space required by the SFC; output Q_i must not be conflated with the input, and when supply is insufficient or equal, Q_i=x_i^*.","In oversupply, Q_i=max(0,x_i^*−η_i), where η_i is a nonnegative oversupply burden; retain the zero-truncation operation and the energy storage measurement unit not specified by this group of evidence.","The main text adopts equal burden: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)/(J−1).","Reserve-price-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)r_i/Σ_i r_i.","Shared-quantity-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)x_i^*/Σ_i x_i^*.","The sum of burdens equaling the oversupply quantity does not guarantee that total allocation after zero truncation equals total demand; no additional reallocation algorithm is supplemented."],["Applies only to order pairs in the same target time slot t that satisfy π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}; no quantity formula for price-incompatible cases is supplied.","Community CDA processes target-time-slot orders during the Agreement Period; the energy unit is kWh, and the quotation unit is £/kWh.","The declared domain of σ_{matched,t} is nonnegative transacted energy; the input order quantities have no explicitly complete numerical bounds, and no common quantity domain is added.","In the main text, the demand residual is updated to σ_{b,t}−σ_{s,t} when σ_{b,t}>σ_{s,t}; the supply residual is updated to σ_{s,t}−σ_{b,t} when σ_{b,t}\u003cσ_{s,t}.","The main text specifies removal of fully matched orders; the appendix else includes the equality case, written as updating the sell order to zero and removing the buy order. The two maintenance formulations are retained separately; the parent class does not unify order maintenance in the equal-quantity case."]],"members":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"The auctioneer performs local allocation by allocating ES spaces for sharing to each SFC according to the auction's allocation rule. Scope: Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. Determination of the participating RU and SFC trading groups precedes execution of the storage allocation rule. Scope: The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. Matching total ES demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction requires selecting J −1 RUs and K −1 SFCs for joint sharing. Scope: Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. Condition: A truthful auction is required, and the determination rule has established J and K. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its entire equilibrium offered amount. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs is less than or equal to total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its equilibrium offered amount minus its assigned oversupply burden, truncated at zero. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs exceeds total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each participating RU bears an equal oversupply burden, calculated as total excess ES divided by J −1. Scope: Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES. Each RU is assigned an oversupply burden proportional to its reservation price. Scope: The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the reservation-price-proportional alternative is used. Replacing the reservation price with the equilibrium offered ES amount in rule (17) assigns each RU an oversupply burden proportional to its shared ES amount. Scope: The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the ES-quantity-proportional variant is used.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. | Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. | Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. | Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. | The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. | The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. | The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C008"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"19c74de6f6ed94069c2396d45ef86dbcc553a6c8d3b97289569421da28a6af65","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"Updating a partially matched demand bid is conditional on the local allocation outcome: its remaining requested quantity becomes σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}. Scope: Residual demand-bid updates in the CDA order book for time slot t during the corresponding Agreement Period. Condition: The demand bid is not fully matched and σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0. A submitted demand bid is removed from the order book when local allocation has fully matched it. Scope: Removal of completed demand bids from the CDA order book for time slot t. Condition: The demand bid is fully matched. A customer with positive optimized net load submits a demand bid with the electricity amount to be bought equal to NL_{i,t}^*. Scope: Community customers submitting demand bids during the CDA Agreement Period corresponding to time slot t in Target Time Period T. Condition: NL_{i,t}^* > 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Community customers submitting demand bids during the CDA Agreement Period corresponding to time slot t in Target Time Period T. | Removal of completed demand bids from the CDA order book for time slot t. | Residual demand-bid updates in the CDA order book for time slot t during the corresponding Agreement Period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g04-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"c2a30ad81613ce70114c65210650d253993db21d696e65b2dbd025d8be9d29c1","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","anchor":false},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"When local allocation leaves an ask partially unmatched, its offered quantity is updated to σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The ask is partially allocated: σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0. When the bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity in a successful CDA match, the fully allocated ask is removed from the order book. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The matched bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity: σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"0aa11f7ed9d844aa9b583a7353c3a90589d8eca0cb80ce6f337a71d76a6da121","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","anchor":false},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The submitted demand quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}. The submitted supply quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"9dece1139b7536d22e42195186aab2a4cda8e3cb233b132bde2449fab8ff8ef0","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003","node_id":"clearing.local","function":"clearing.local","unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"no on Fig. 3. Determination of the Vickrey price, the maximum auction price, and To the number of pa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"ual fashion where each time slot has a suitable time duration based on the type of application, e.g.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To this end, we propose that, once J and K are determined, K −1 SFCs and J −1 RUs will be engaged in the joint ES sharing process, which is a necessary condition for matching total demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction scheme [44].","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"To this end, we propose that, once J and K are determined, K −1 SFCs and J −1 RUs will be engaged in the joint ES sharing process, which is a necessary condition for matching total demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction scheme [44]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"from the bounded range [0, bi] in order to maximize its utility ve function Ui. To that end, due to ","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Q_i(\\mathbf{x}) = \\begin{cases} x_i^* & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* \\le \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\\\ (x_i^* − \\eta_i)^+ & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* > \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\end{cases} (16) where (f)^+ = \\max(0,f) and \\eta_i is the allotment of the excess ES \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m that an RU i must endure. Essentially, the rule in (16) emphasizes that if the requirements of the SFCs exceed the available ES space from the RUs, each RU i will allow the SFCs to share all of the ES x_i that it put into the market. However, if the available ES exceeds the total demand by the SFCs, then each RU i will have to share a fraction of the oversupply \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"Q_i(\\mathbf{x}) = \\begin{cases} x_i^* & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* \\le \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\\\ (x_i^* − \\eta_i)^+ & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* > \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\end{cases} (16) where (f)^+ = \\max(0,f) and \\eta_i is the allotment of the excess ES \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m that an RU i must endure. Essentially, the rule in (16) emphasizes that if the requirements of the SFCs exceed the available ES space from the RUs, each RU i will allow the SFCs to share all of the ES x_i that it put into the market. However, if the available ES exceeds the total demand by the SFCs, then each RU i will have to share a fraction of the oversupply \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"By replacing ri with x∗i in (17), the burden allocation can be Th determined in proportion to the sh","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to equal allocation [44], each RU bears an equal burden η_i = \\frac{1}{J −1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m\\right), i = [1, 2, ..., J −1] (18) of the oversupply.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"According to equal allocation [44], each RU bears an equal burden η_i = \\frac{1}{J −1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m\\right), i = [1, 2, ..., J −1] (18) of the oversupply."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"mechanisms in energy markets. Therefore, we will use equal fa allocation of (18) for the rest of the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here it is important to note that, although proportional allocation allows the distribution of oversupply according to some properties of the RUs, equal allocation is more suitable to make the auction scheme strategy proof [44]. Strategy proofness is important for designing auction mechanisms as it encourages the participating players not to lie about their private information such as reservation price [41], which is essential for the acceptability and sustainability of such mechanisms in energy markets. Therefore, we will use equal allocation of (18) for the rest of the paper.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"Here it is important to note that, although proportional allocation allows the distribution of oversupply according to some properties of the RUs, equal allocation is more suitable to make the auction scheme strategy proof [44]. Strategy proofness is important for designing auction mechanisms as it encourages the participating players not to lie about their private information such as reservation price [41], which is essential for the acceptability and sustainability of such mechanisms in energy markets. Therefore, we will use equal allocation of (18) for the rest of the paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"TUSHAR et al.: ES SHARING IN SMART GRID: A MODIFIED AUCTION-BASED APPRO price6 ri of each RU. Altern","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In proportional allocation [47], a fraction of the total burden η_i is allocated to each RU i in proportion to the reservation price r_i (or, x_i^*) such that Σ_i η_i = Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − Σ_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, which can be implemented as follows: η_i = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m) r_i}{\\sum_i r_i}, i = [1, 2, ..., J −1]. (17) By replacing r_i with x_i^* in (17), the burden allocation can be determined in proportion to the shared ES by each RU.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"In proportional allocation [47], a fraction of the total burden η_i is allocated to each RU i in proportion to the reservation price r_i (or, x_i^*) such that Σ_i η_i = Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − Σ_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, which can be implemented as follows: η_i = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m) r_i}{\\sum_i r_i}, i = [1, 2, ..., J −1]. (17) By replacing r_i with x_i^* in (17), the burden allocation can be determined in proportion to the shared ES by each RU."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p15-c1r1__v141-a-M01-matching","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. (continued) CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agre 7: make the tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p15-c1r1__v141-a-M01-matching","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. (continued) CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agre 7: make the tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}).","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p14-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"welfare of the whole community with the proposed P2P energy trading and residual balancing mechanism","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agreements\n1: while the current time is within the Agreement Period for CDA\n2: if a bid/ask associated with the time slot t arrives at the exchange\n3: put the bid/ask in the order book t (sorted by the bid/ask price);\n4: for any pair of bid o_{b,t} and ask o_{s,t} in the order book t\n5: if π_{b,t} >= π_{s,t}\n6: match the following amount of electricity: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t});","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agreements\n1: while the current time is within the Agreement Period for CDA\n2: if a bid/ask associated with the time slot t arrives at the exchange\n3: put the bid/ask in the order book t (sorted by the bid/ask price);\n4: for any pair of bid o_{b,t} and ask o_{s,t} in the order book t\n5: if π_{b,t} >= π_{s,t}\n6: match the following amount of electricity: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t});"}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["matched_quantity_allocation","quantity_allocation_with_oversupply_rationing"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L5-f2595785bb","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L5","ontological_kind":"quantity_allocation_with_oversupply_rationing"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Under the trading scope and matching premises specified by the source, supply acceptance is determined by comparing supply and demand quantities: when there is no excess supply, the full amount is accepted; when there is excess supply, the actual allocated quantity is determined according to the curtailment rule for that scope.","object":"The allocation relationship from declared or equilibrium supply quantity to actual allocated quantity for supply resources; the energy storage sharing space and order electricity quantity retain their respective types, units, and aggregation scopes.","inputs":"Comparable supply quantities, demand quantities, applicable premises, and source-specified oversupply handling parameters within the same trading scope.","operation":"Within that scope, when supply does not exceed demand, all supply is accepted; when supply exceeds demand, the actual allocated quantity is calculated according to the source-specified oversupply curtailment rules.","outputs":"The actual allocated quantity on the supply side, retaining the distinct output semantics and quantity domains of each RU's shared quantity and the bilateral transaction volumes of an order pair.","boundary":"Limited to L5/DA quantity configuration; energy storage compares the total quantity of the selected group, and CDA compares price-compatible order pairs. One must not infer a common max/min formula, that total group allocation necessarily equals demand, per-demand-side allocation, or common order maintenance rules."},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"The auctioneer performs local allocation by allocating ES spaces for sharing to each SFC according to the auction's allocation rule. Scope: Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. Determination of the participating RU and SFC trading groups precedes execution of the storage allocation rule. Scope: The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. Matching total ES demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction requires selecting J −1 RUs and K −1 SFCs for joint sharing. Scope: Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. Condition: A truthful auction is required, and the determination rule has established J and K. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its entire equilibrium offered amount. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs is less than or equal to total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its equilibrium offered amount minus its assigned oversupply burden, truncated at zero. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs exceeds total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each participating RU bears an equal oversupply burden, calculated as total excess ES divided by J −1. Scope: Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES. Each RU is assigned an oversupply burden proportional to its reservation price. Scope: The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the reservation-price-proportional alternative is used. Replacing the reservation price with the equilibrium offered ES amount in rule (17) assigns each RU an oversupply burden proportional to its shared ES amount. Scope: The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the ES-quantity-proportional variant is used.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. | Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. | Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. | Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. | The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. | The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. | The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C008"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"19c74de6f6ed94069c2396d45ef86dbcc553a6c8d3b97289569421da28a6af65"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auctioneer performs local allocation by allocating ES spaces for sharing to each SFC according to the auction's allocation rule. Scope: Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Determination of the participating RU and SFC trading groups precedes execution of the storage allocation rule. Scope: The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E26"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"no on Fig. 3. Determination of the Vickrey price, the maximum auction price, and To the number of pa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"ual fashion where each time slot has a suitable time duration based on the type of application, e.g.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Matching total ES demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction requires selecting J −1 RUs and K −1 SFCs for joint sharing. Scope: Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. Condition: A truthful auction is required, and the determination rule has established J and K.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"To this end, we propose that, once J and K are determined, K −1 SFCs and J −1 RUs will be engaged in the joint ES sharing process, which is a necessary condition for matching total demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction scheme [44]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its entire equilibrium offered amount. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs is less than or equal to total ES requested by the participating SFCs.","expression":"Q_i = x_i^{*} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i^{*} \\le \\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} q_m","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-Qi"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"from the bounded range [0, bi] in order to maximize its utility ve function Ui. To that end, due to ","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Q_i(\\mathbf{x}) = \\begin{cases} x_i^* & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* \\le \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\\\ (x_i^* − \\eta_i)^+ & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* > \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\end{cases} (16) where (f)^+ = \\max(0,f) and \\eta_i is the allotment of the excess ES \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m that an RU i must endure. Essentially, the rule in (16) emphasizes that if the requirements of the SFCs exceed the available ES space from the RUs, each RU i will allow the SFCs to share all of the ES x_i that it put into the market. However, if the available ES exceeds the total demand by the SFCs, then each RU i will have to share a fraction of the oversupply \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its equilibrium offered amount minus its assigned oversupply burden, truncated at zero. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs exceeds total ES requested by the participating SFCs.","expression":"Q_i = \\left(x_i^{*} - \\eta_i\\right)^{+} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i^{*} > \\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} q_m,\\quad (f)^{+}=\\max(0,f)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-Qi","v141-c-R001-x-etai"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"from the bounded range [0, bi] in order to maximize its utility ve function Ui. To that end, due to ","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Q_i(\\mathbf{x}) = \\begin{cases} x_i^* & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* \\le \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\\\ (x_i^* − \\eta_i)^+ & \\text{if } \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* > \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, \\end{cases} (16) where (f)^+ = \\max(0,f) and \\eta_i is the allotment of the excess ES \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m that an RU i must endure. Essentially, the rule in (16) emphasizes that if the requirements of the SFCs exceed the available ES space from the RUs, each RU i will allow the SFCs to share all of the ES x_i that it put into the market. However, if the available ES exceeds the total demand by the SFCs, then each RU i will have to share a fraction of the oversupply \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each participating RU bears an equal oversupply burden, calculated as total excess ES divided by J −1. Scope: Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES.","expression":"\\eta_i = \\frac{1}{J-1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i^{*} - \\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} q_m\\right),\\quad i=1,\\dots,J-1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-etai"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"By replacing ri with x∗i in (17), the burden allocation can be Th determined in proportion to the sh","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to equal allocation [44], each RU bears an equal burden η_i = \\frac{1}{J −1}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m\\right), i = [1, 2, ..., J −1] (18) of the oversupply."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"mechanisms in energy markets. Therefore, we will use equal fa allocation of (18) for the rest of the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here it is important to note that, although proportional allocation allows the distribution of oversupply according to some properties of the RUs, equal allocation is more suitable to make the auction scheme strategy proof [44]. Strategy proofness is important for designing auction mechanisms as it encourages the participating players not to lie about their private information such as reservation price [41], which is essential for the acceptability and sustainability of such mechanisms in energy markets. Therefore, we will use equal allocation of (18) for the rest of the paper."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each RU is assigned an oversupply burden proportional to its reservation price. Scope: The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the reservation-price-proportional alternative is used.","expression":"\\eta_i = \\frac{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i^{*} - \\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} q_m\\right) r_i}{\\sum_i r_i},\\quad i=1,\\dots,J-1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-etai"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R001-theta-ri","v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"TUSHAR et al.: ES SHARING IN SMART GRID: A MODIFIED AUCTION-BASED APPRO price6 ri of each RU. Altern","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In proportional allocation [47], a fraction of the total burden η_i is allocated to each RU i in proportion to the reservation price r_i (or, x_i^*) such that Σ_i η_i = Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − Σ_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, which can be implemented as follows: η_i = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m) r_i}{\\sum_i r_i}, i = [1, 2, ..., J −1]. (17) By replacing r_i with x_i^* in (17), the burden allocation can be determined in proportion to the shared ES by each RU."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C008","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Replacing the reservation price with the equilibrium offered ES amount in rule (17) assigns each RU an oversupply burden proportional to its shared ES amount. Scope: The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the ES-quantity-proportional variant is used.","expression":"\\eta_i = \\frac{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} x_i^{*} - \\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} q_m\\right) x_i^{*}}{\\sum_i x_i^{*}},\\quad i=1,\\dots,J-1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-etai"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","v141-c-R001-theta-qm","v141-c-R001-theta-J","v141-c-R001-theta-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-D. Allocation Rule","anchor_text":"TUSHAR et al.: ES SHARING IN SMART GRID: A MODIFIED AUCTION-BASED APPRO price6 ri of each RU. Altern","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In proportional allocation [47], a fraction of the total burden η_i is allocated to each RU i in proportion to the reservation price r_i (or, x_i^*) such that Σ_i η_i = Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − Σ_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m, which can be implemented as follows: η_i = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^* − \\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} q_m) r_i}{\\sum_i r_i}, i = [1, 2, ..., J −1]. (17) By replacing r_i with x_i^* in (17), the burden allocation can be determined in proportion to the shared ES by each RU."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-Qi","symbol":"Q_i","meaning":"ES amount allocated to be jointly shared by RU i and the SFCs under allocation rule (16).","kind":"operational","domain":"Allocated ES amount for participating RU i; determined by the piecewise allocation rule in (16).","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Qi"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-x-etai","symbol":"\\eta_i","meaning":"Oversupply burden (excess-ES allotment) assigned to participating RU i.","kind":"operational","domain":"Nonnegative burden share assigned to RU i; in the adopted equal-allocation rule it is the total excess ES divided by J-1.","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-etai"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star","symbol":"x_i^{*}","meaning":"Equilibrium amount of ES offered for sharing by participating RU i, used as an input to the clearing allocation rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-xi-star"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-qm","symbol":"q_m","meaning":"ES space required by participating SFC m, used as demand input to the clearing allocation rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-qm"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-J","symbol":"J","meaning":"Number of participating RUs determined by the determination rule; allocation formulas use the J-1 participating RUs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-J"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-K","symbol":"K","meaning":"Number of participating SFCs determined by the determination rule; allocation formulas use the K-1 participating SFCs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-K"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-theta-ri","symbol":"r_i","meaning":"Reservation price per unit of energy declared by RU i, used in the reservation-price-proportional oversupply allocation alternative.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"price per unit of energy","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-ri"}]},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","paper_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","function":"clearing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"Updating a partially matched demand bid is conditional on the local allocation outcome: its remaining requested quantity becomes σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}. Scope: Residual demand-bid updates in the CDA order book for time slot t during the corresponding Agreement Period. Condition: The demand bid is not fully matched and σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0. A submitted demand bid is removed from the order book when local allocation has fully matched it. Scope: Removal of completed demand bids from the CDA order book for time slot t. Condition: The demand bid is fully matched. A customer with positive optimized net load submits a demand bid with the electricity amount to be bought equal to NL_{i,t}^*. Scope: Community customers submitting demand bids during the CDA Agreement Period corresponding to time slot t in Target Time Period T. Condition: NL_{i,t}^* > 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Community customers submitting demand bids during the CDA Agreement Period corresponding to time slot t in Target Time Period T. | Removal of completed demand bids from the CDA order book for time slot t. | Residual demand-bid updates in the CDA order book for time slot t during the corresponding Agreement Period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g04-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"c2a30ad81613ce70114c65210650d253993db21d696e65b2dbd025d8be9d29c1"},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"When local allocation leaves an ask partially unmatched, its offered quantity is updated to σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The ask is partially allocated: σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0. When the bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity in a successful CDA match, the fully allocated ask is removed from the order book. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The matched bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity: σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"0aa11f7ed9d844aa9b583a7353c3a90589d8eca0cb80ce6f337a71d76a6da121"},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The submitted demand quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}. The submitted supply quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"9dece1139b7536d22e42195186aab2a4cda8e3cb233b132bde2449fab8ff8ef0"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Updating a partially matched demand bid is conditional on the local allocation outcome: its remaining requested quantity becomes σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}. Scope: Residual demand-bid updates in the CDA order book for time slot t during the corresponding Agreement Period. Condition: The demand bid is not fully matched and σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0.","expression":"σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} − σ_{s,t} if σ_{b,t} − σ_{s,t} > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001-X002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p15-c1r1__v141-a-M01-matching","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. (continued) CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agre 7: make the tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"A submitted demand bid is removed from the order book when local allocation has fully matched it. Scope: Removal of completed demand bids from the CDA order book for time slot t. Condition: The demand bid is fully matched.","expression":"σ_{b,t} ≤ σ_{s,t} ⇒ the demand order for (b,t) is removed from the order book for time slot t","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p15-c1r1__v141-a-M01-matching","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. (continued) CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agre 7: make the tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"When local allocation leaves an ask partially unmatched, its offered quantity is updated to σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The ask is partially allocated: σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0.","expression":"\\sigma_{b,t} - \\sigma_{s,t} \u003c 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\sigma'_{s,t} = \\sigma_{s,t} - \\sigma_{b,t}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x001","v141-c-R002-x002","v141-c-R002-x003"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"When the bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity in a successful CDA match, the fully allocated ask is removed from the order book. Scope: CDA order-book maintenance following a successful match for time slot t in the Target Time Period T. Condition: The matched bid quantity exceeds the ask quantity: σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}.","expression":"\\sigma_{b,t} > \\sigma_{s,t} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\text{the ask is fully allocated and removed from the order book}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x001","v141-c-R002-x002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order book, and the bid/ask that is not fully matched will be updated by o'_{b,t} = (b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} > 0, (4) o'_{s,t} = (s_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) if σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t} \u003c 0, (5) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t}, (6) σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t}. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p15-c1r1__v141-a-M01-matching","page":15,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. (continued) CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agre 7: make the tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-15.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"8: if σ_{b,t} > σ_{s,t}\n9: modify the bid as o'_{b,t} = o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ'_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}) where σ'_{b,t} = σ_{b,t} - σ_{s,t};\n10: remove the ask o_{s,t} from the order book;\n11: else\n12: modify the ask as o'_{s,t} = o_{s,t}(b_t, π_{s,t}, σ'_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}) where σ'_{s,t} = σ_{s,t} - σ_{b,t};\n13: remove the bid o_{b,t} from the order book;\n14: end if\n15: end if\n16: end for\n17: end if\n18: end while"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The submitted demand quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}.","expression":"\\pi_{b,t} \\ge \\pi_{s,t} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\sigma_{matched,t} = \\min(\\sigma_{b,t}, \\sigma_{s,t})","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_sigma_matched_t","x_sigma_b_t","x_sigma_s_t","x_pi_b_t","x_pi_s_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g04-E01"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p14-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"welfare of the whole community with the proposed P2P energy trading and residual balancing mechanism","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agreements\n1: while the current time is within the Agreement Period for CDA\n2: if a bid/ask associated with the time slot t arrives at the exchange\n3: put the bid/ask in the order book t (sorted by the bid/ask price);\n4: for any pair of bid o_{b,t} and ask o_{s,t} in the order book t\n5: if π_{b,t} >= π_{s,t}\n6: match the following amount of electricity: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t});"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The submitted supply quantity supplies an input to local allocation: the matched electricity quantity is min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}). Scope: Within the community's CDA Agreement Period, for a bid and ask in the order book for target time slot t. Condition: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}.","expression":"\\pi_{b,t} \\ge \\pi_{s,t} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\sigma_{matched,t} = \\min(\\sigma_{b,t}, \\sigma_{s,t})","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_sigma_matched_t","x_sigma_b_t","x_sigma_s_t","x_pi_b_t","x_pi_s_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g04-E01"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p14-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix A","anchor_text":"welfare of the whole community with the proposed P2P energy trading and residual balancing mechanism","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"CDA process for customers to reach P2P energy trading agreements\n1: while the current time is within the Agreement Period for CDA\n2: if a bid/ask associated with the time slot t arrives at the exchange\n3: put the bid/ask in the order book t (sorted by the bid/ask price);\n4: for any pair of bid o_{b,t} and ask o_{s,t} in the order book t\n5: if π_{b,t} >= π_{s,t}\n6: match the following amount of electricity: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t});"}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X001","symbol":"σ_{b,t}","meaning":"Electricity quantity requested by the demand bid o_{b,t} for time slot t, as defined in the order descriptor.","kind":"operational","domain":"kWh amount of electricity requested in a submitted demand bid; the source gives no explicit numeric bound on the supplied pages","unit":"kWh","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X002","symbol":"σ'_{b,t}","meaning":"Remaining requested quantity of a partially matched demand bid after local allocation for time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"kWh residual demand quantity produced by the order-book update; the source gives no explicit numeric bound","unit":"kWh","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-x001","symbol":"\\sigma_{b,t}","meaning":"Quantity of electricity requested in the bid o_{b,t} for time slot t, used in the R002 ask-update condition.","kind":"operational","domain":"Order quantity in kWh in the CDA order book for time slot t; the supplied evidence does not state a sign restriction.","unit":"kWh","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E09"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-x002","symbol":"\\sigma_{s,t}","meaning":"Quantity of electricity offered in the ask o_{s,t} for time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Order quantity in kWh in the CDA order book for time slot t; the supplied evidence does not state a sign restriction.","unit":"kWh","indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E09"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x002"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R002-x003","symbol":"\\sigma'_{s,t}","meaning":"Updated quantity remaining in the partially matched ask after subtracting the matched bid quantity.","kind":"operational","domain":"Updated ask order quantity in kWh for time slot t; under the stated condition σ'_{s,t}=σ_{s,t}-σ_{b,t} is positive.","unit":"kWh","indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x003"},{"variable_id":"x_sigma_matched_t","symbol":"σ_{matched,t}","meaning":"Matched electricity quantity for a compatible bid-ask pair in the order book for target time slot t; the clearing relation determines it as min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}).","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative matched electricity quantity in kWh for target time slot t; exact numeric bounds are not stated in the supplied clearing quotation","unit":"kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g04-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_matched_t"},{"variable_id":"x_sigma_b_t","symbol":"σ_{b,t}","meaning":"Submitted demand-bid electricity quantity in the order book for target time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity in kWh for target time slot t; exact numeric bounds are not stated in the supplied clearing quotation","unit":"kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_b_t"},{"variable_id":"x_sigma_s_t","symbol":"σ_{s,t}","meaning":"Submitted supply-ask electricity quantity in the order book for target time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"electricity quantity in kWh for target time slot t; exact numeric bounds are not stated in the supplied clearing quotation","unit":"kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_s_t"},{"variable_id":"x_pi_b_t","symbol":"π_{b,t}","meaning":"Demand-bid price submitted for target time slot t, used in the price-compatibility condition for local allocation.","kind":"operational","domain":"price in £/kWh for target time slot t; exact numeric bounds are not stated in the supplied clearing quotation","unit":"£/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::x::x_pi_b_t"},{"variable_id":"x_pi_s_t","symbol":"π_{s,t}","meaning":"Supply-ask price submitted for target time slot t, used in the price-compatibility condition for local allocation.","kind":"operational","domain":"price in £/kWh for target time slot t; exact numeric bounds are not stated in the supplied clearing quotation","unit":"£/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::x::x_pi_s_t"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-T001","symbol":"σ_{s,t}","meaning":"Electricity quantity of the matched seller ask o_{s,t} used in the demand-bid residual update for time slot t; for this demand-submission rule it is the clearing-side ask quantity entering the update condition.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"symbolic ask-order quantity; no numeric value is supplied in the source"},"unit":"kWh","indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","stage":"L5","subtype":"quantity_allocation_with_oversupply_rationing","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"Determine the energy storage quantity Q_i actually shared by each selected RU: when Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*≤Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m, Q_i=x_i^*; in oversupply, Q_i=max(0,x_i^*−η_i), where η_i is the oversupply burden allocated to that RU.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: shared energy storage supply of selected suppliers and demand of demand sides.","Core operation: accept supply according to the comparison of total supply and demand, or deduct the oversupply burden and take a nonnegative value.","Output: the actual shared allocation quantity Q_i of each supplier."],"variation_fields":["Suppliers are J−1 RUs, and demand sides are K−1 SFCs; allocation is executed after the group is determined.","Adopt equal burden sharing: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)/(J−1).","Reserve-price-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)r_i/Σ_i r_i.","Shared-quantity-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)x_i^*/Σ_i x_i^*.","Repeatedly apply the same allocation rule in the time-slot extension."],"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C008"],"paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"clearing.local","template_code":"DA"},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","stage":"L5","subtype":"matched_quantity_allocation","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"For candidate buy and sell orders that are price-compatible, when π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}, the transacted energy is σ_{matched,t}=min(σ_{b,t},σ_{s,t}).","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: candidate buy and sell orders in the same time slot.","Core relation: when prices are compatible, allocate according to the smaller quantity of the two sides.","Output: transacted energy σ_{matched,t}."],"variation_fields":["Community CDA and target time slot t; the energy unit is kWh.","Transaction results are used to update residual order quantities and remove completed orders.","Order maintenance details retain the respective conditions of the main text and the appendix."],"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001"],"paper_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","function":"clearing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","source_definition":"Determine the energy storage quantity Q_i actually shared by each selected RU: when Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*≤Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m, Q_i=x_i^*; in oversupply, Q_i=max(0,x_i^*−η_i), where η_i is the oversupply burden allocated to that RU.","retained_variants":["The object is the energy storage sharing space provided by J−1 RUs and demanded by K−1 SFCs; the group is determined first, then allocation is executed, with repeated application in the time-slot extension.","Input x_i^* is the equilibrium provision quantity, and q_m is the energy storage space required by the SFC; output Q_i must not be conflated with the input, and when supply is insufficient or equal, Q_i=x_i^*.","In oversupply, Q_i=max(0,x_i^*−η_i), where η_i is a nonnegative oversupply burden; retain the zero-truncation operation and the energy storage measurement unit not specified by this group of evidence.","The main text adopts equal burden: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)/(J−1).","Reserve-price-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)r_i/Σ_i r_i.","Shared-quantity-proportional alternative: η_i=(Σ_{i=1}^{J−1}x_i^*−Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}q_m)x_i^*/Σ_i x_i^*.","The sum of burdens equaling the oversupply quantity does not guarantee that total allocation after zero truncation equals total demand; no additional reallocation algorithm is supplemented."],"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C008"]},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::clearing.local","source_definition":"For candidate buy and sell orders that are price-compatible, when π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}, the transacted energy is σ_{matched,t}=min(σ_{b,t},σ_{s,t}).","retained_variants":["Applies only to order pairs in the same target time slot t that satisfy π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}; no quantity formula for price-incompatible cases is supplied.","Community CDA processes target-time-slot orders during the Agreement Period; the energy unit is kWh, and the quotation unit is £/kWh.","The declared domain of σ_{matched,t} is nonnegative transacted energy; the input order quantities have no explicitly complete numerical bounds, and no common quantity domain is added.","In the main text, the demand residual is updated to σ_{b,t}−σ_{s,t} when σ_{b,t}>σ_{s,t}; the supply residual is updated to σ_{s,t}−σ_{b,t} when σ_{b,t}\u003cσ_{s,t}.","The main text specifies removal of fully matched orders; the appendix else includes the equality case, written as updating the sell order to zero and removing the buy order. The two maintenance formulations are retained separately; the parent class does not unify order maintenance in the equal-quantity case."],"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002"]}],"source_parent_definition":{"definition":"Under the trading scope and matching premises specified by the source, supply acceptance is determined by comparing supply and demand quantities: when there is no excess supply, the full amount is accepted; when there is excess supply, the actual allocated quantity is determined according to the curtailment rule for that scope.","object":"The allocation relationship from declared or equilibrium supply quantity to actual allocated quantity for supply resources; the energy storage sharing space and order electricity quantity retain their respective types, units, and aggregation scopes.","inputs":"Comparable supply quantities, demand quantities, applicable premises, and source-specified oversupply handling parameters within the same trading scope.","operation":"Within that scope, when supply does not exceed demand, all supply is accepted; when supply exceeds demand, the actual allocated quantity is calculated according to the source-specified oversupply curtailment rules.","outputs":"The actual allocated quantity on the supply side, retaining the distinct output semantics and quantity domains of each RU's shared quantity and the bilateral transaction volumes of an order pair.","boundary":"Limited to L5/DA quantity configuration; energy storage compares the total quantity of the selected group, and CDA compares price-compatible order pairs. One must not infer a common max/min formula, that total group allocation necessarily equals demand, per-demand-side allocation, or common order maintenance rules."},"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/247"});
